								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11499#msg11499">Re: Parents.. a little help plz..</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #24 on:</b> September 30, 2004, 11:10:38 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I didn&#039;t have the smeer poop problem with my first two (hopefully not with the upcoming one either).<br /><br />We just finished potty training the second one (she&#039;s about 2 1/2), for over 2 months, she would sit on the potty, pull up her panties then poop in them. She refused to poop in the potty. This lead to a couple of &quot;what&#039;s this daddy?&quot; <br /><br />ps. isn&#039;t it fun trying to get poop out from under fingernails?
						</td>
					</tr>
